    {
      "id": "method-swap-round-trips-through-the-raw-equivalent",
      "why": "The double conversion, and the subtlest case in the corpus. Boiled 64 g -> raw equivalent 64/0.85 = 75.294 -> grilled 75.294*0.7 = 52.706 -> 53 g. Rounding happens ONCE, at the end: rounding the intermediate to 75 first also gives 53 here but drifts on other factor pairs. measuredState stays \"cooked\" — this branch does not touch it.",
      "input": {
        "ingredient": {
          "id": "rice-fixture",
          "label": "riz",
          "ingredientId": "rice",
          "cookingMethod": "boiled",
          "quantity": 64,
